      "content": "i get that. the idea of just... giving in to the darkness. it's something i've been thinking about a lot lately too. like, what if the most honest way to write him is to show that the relief only comes when he actually goes through with it? that the struggle is just prolonging the inevitable? it feels like the only way he truly gains control over his life is by deciding when it's over.",
